{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/237367-splintered-city-seattle-discussion-thread","id":237367,"title":"Splintered City: Seattle Discussion Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-22T14:38:01-07:00","id":237367,"title":"Splintered City: Seattle Discussion Thread","content":"With the Kickstarter backer release of Splintered City: Seattle I wanted to start gushing about it but didn't want to clog up the errata thread, so here we are.<br /> <br /> So far this book is awesome! As one of the 'coffee fueled coders that works on the East Side' it is super fun to see this whole area put through the lens of Demon (and others when I get that far).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T16:07:51-07:00","id":237478,"title":"","content":"Oh my word, the picture on page 62 is fantastic! <br /> This book as a whole seems far more useful than any other WW/OP citybook. It has a central theme - the time splinters, a ton of npc statblocks, an adventure section, and a whole chapter on plothooks for all the other gamelines. Best of all, not all of those plothooks bring changlings, werewolves, etc into the content from the rest of the book. Rather, they focus on fitting each gameline into the mood of paranoia that suffuses the rest of the book. <br /> <br /> Several mechanical thumbs up for this book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T17:55:03-07:00","id":237581,"title":"","content":"That opening fiction is absolutely stellar and does an amazing job of showing how those elements of the setting would work in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T22:10:52-07:00","id":237770,"title":"","content":"I don't care if its a ripoff of <i>Skin Game</i>, I'm having a crossover game for the Apocalypse Vault.<br /> <br /> And I think I'll get stupidly anticipatory and have a Beast fill in Nicky's shoes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T23:17:50-07:00","id":237935,"title":"","content":"<i>one</i> demon, it forms an impression. It normalizes this idea, gives it ground. Some valid interpretations of DtD, I think, for which the demonic state is an important statement about freedom, suffer as a result. It can also accidentally communicate to Storytellers that this is something that is normal and casually okay to drop on a player character as well, when that decision ought to be more careful and given thought before being done. (I won't say it can't be done well, but you really have to know your player and what they want out of the game to pull that reveal off.) The extension that the God-Machine's plan goes all the way into Y2K's everyday life as a demon today takes this idea into silly town for me; as vast as the GM is, it's hard to swallow that it could keep an accurate forecast that far ahead. It does the things that I said earlier about &quot;forming an impression,&quot; but much more so.<br /> <br /> - The decision not to give the Gerent any stats at all. Stats are relevant for more than combat, and sometimes are referenced by abilities the players use. Some kind of guidelines for what happens if the shit really goes down would be nice too, really. Feels like a cop-out.<br /> <br /> Okay, when I write it out in that much detail, it looks like it's more than it is. That's three things. Stayin' honest. Here's stuff I did like, not necessarily a comprehensive list:<br /> <br /> - My God, that cover. Who drew that cover? Give that person more work, it's so well composed and hangs together well. Kudos to whoever designed the title logo for the supplement, too. They complement one another and it's a good logo just by its own merits.<br /> <br /> - The Luther Burbank Lid is a nice example of infrastructure that is relatively benign. I like that that's there.<br /> <br /> - The extended treatment of just how stable or real the 1889 world is. I especially love the spot parties. That's a fun way to spin your average ominous-anomalies hook.<br /> <br /> - Marc Janssen's projects. Good color combined with a sincere-feeling story about how stigmata would affect a relatively normal person.<br /> <br /> - Local Curiosities. I love these sidebars. Fantastic flavor, a lot can be done with so few words. Do more of these, please. Give whichever writer decided to put these in a cookie. Thin mint.<br /> <br /> - Pacific Tower. Cool, versatile concept.<br /> <br /> - Pike Place Flowers. It was interesting up until the last sentence, which is brilliant. There's enough detail that if it doesn't give you ideas Pike Place is still a useful hook, but it's so vague that it can go in all sorts of directions.<br /> <br /> - Mr. Excitement is cool, and her demonic form description is fantastic.<br /> <br /> - Bait and Hound. Nice concept made into a great aesthetic victory by both the descriptions given by the writer and the interpretations then made by the illustrator. Look at these guys. Man.<br /> <br /> - Stray. I like having the occasional genuinely friendly and receptive NPC, and I'm a sucker for talking animals. Great-Grandfather Crow is one of my favorite Promethean NPCs, too.<br /> <br /> - The idea of the Apocalypse Vault itself is okay, but the writeup takes the exact right approach to it when its first suggestion on how to use in a game is to run a <i>heist</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T23:24:23-07:00","id":237941,"title":"","content":"I guess the forum just eats the first part of your post if it's too long? Append this to the beginning:<br /> <br /> &quot;Really good, densely packed supplement. Here's the stuff I didn't like:<br /> <br /> - The coffee shop infrastructure feels like it's trying much too hard to be clever telling an old joke. It also feels a little too pervasive in reach and effect, between the wide distribution of the coffee chains and the writeup going as far as to suggest they might put drugs in the coffee to make the populace pliable and manipulable. This hook feels like it would be much more at home in the cWoD as a Technocracy project or somesuch.<br /> - The idea that Y2K's entire Descent, from his Fall to his current everyday life, is the result of a grand game by the God-Machine to the ends of monitoring the Vault. This is tricky territory. The idea that the God-Machine might be at cause over a demon's Fall, that it is an intended function of its angels and works somehow to the Machine's ends, is a useful idea to keep in the game. As an idea. I feel the game suffers once it becomes more than an idea, when the gameline presents a demon who is verifiably an intentional product and pawn of the Machine from beginning to end. Even when this is true of only <i>one</i> demon, it forms an impression.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also notice that the credits page tells us the cover illustration is by Michael Gaydos. Very nice, versatile guy too it looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 08-23-2014, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T00:48:28-07:00","id":238008,"title":"","content":"Really weird bit of love from me; the tiny writeups about what other supernaturals are up to in Seattle was super neat, and I like that they all played with non-standard setups; weak Courts for CtL, a brewing civil war for HtV, etc. Very neat stuff,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T08:00:51-07:00","id":238194,"title":"","content":"The Apocalypse Vault seems interesting but how could it be used in as possible negotiating tool in a setting where a future apocalypse is already assured to happen? would it be kind of like god-machine bartering or a different use for the vault entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:00:07-07:00","id":238294,"title":"","content":"If you're asking as a default setting, the default is that the world doesn't have a set apocalypse-lots of powers, G-M included, are interested in keeping things together.<br /> <br /> If you're asking as a &quot;My game&quot; setting, the Apocalypse Fault becomes less valuable in certain ways, but it's still useful in that it gives you a choice. Trade one End for the other.<br /> <br /> Now why would you do that? Well, some Ends are more survivable than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:32:38-07:00","id":238371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/237367-splintered-city-seattle-discussion-thread?p=238194#post238194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Apocalypse Vault seems interesting but how could it be used in as possible negotiating tool in a setting where a future apocalypse is already assured to happen? would it be kind of like god-machine bartering or a different use for the vault entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Machine has those apocalypses locked away in the Vault because it doesn't want them to happen; stealing one of the spheres and cracking it open not only releases something the Machine sealed away because it didn't like it, it also releases it onto the dominant timeline. That's a Very Bad Thing in the Machine's eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:19:55-07:00","id":238527,"title":"","content":"what i'm trying to get at is &quot;say for example that the characters witnessed a terminator-like apocalypse (or similar unstoppable event) in 20XX before getting sent back in time to the 1999 splinter and trying to breach the vault.&quot; could they use the god-machine bartering option to make the god-machine potentially soften the blow suffered by the apocalypse or would that be beyond the scope of what the apocalypse vault bartering option could do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:12:17-07:00","id":238577,"title":"","content":"It's your game, you decide.<br /> <br /> I would say yes, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T18:24:29-07:00","id":238733,"title":"","content":"so what role could the apocalypse vault play in a setting based on the &quot;survivor from the dark future&quot; archetype? or does the apocalypse vault assume a more &quot;modern&quot; viewpoint for the characters entering the vault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T19:30:03-07:00","id":238786,"title":"","content":"Seriously, it's a matter of just picking a different catastrophe, one they think they can beat.<br /> <br /> And yes, it assumes a more modern viewpoint from the characters. Namely because the game's default setting is 'now', not 'then'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:04:15-07:00","id":240301,"title":"","content":"Actually, from the way it's described, I think the apocalypse vault could provide an antidote for more than just another apocalypse, unleashing an apocalypse seems to lock in that timeline, otherwise it wouldn't stop another apocalypse, it would just mean that the world was facing two apocalypses. <br /> <br /> So I could definitely see desperate PCs breaking into the vault to say, prevent the Prince of 100,000 leaves from rewriting the last 6000 years of human history with glorified cannibalism. <br /> <br /> There are quite possibly several apocalypses in there that would be better than a Donner Party Meal being the best sellers from Mickey D's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T09:44:26-07:00","id":241419,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one that read the opening fiction for the final story-hook chapter and instantly thought of the whole &quot;packet theta from the moon&quot; from the original God-Machine fiction in the first edition WoD corebook opening? <br /> <br /> I even thought that was going to be the object/entity when I saw the title entry &quot;Its Time Has Come&quot;. It turned out to be something...similar but different.<br /> <br /> Still an interesting idea of presenting a possible post-demonic state. Interesting to see if any similar ideas or plot hooks will be explored in the ST Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T16:03:18-08:00","id":303823,"title":"","content":"This book is actually unbelievably good. I mean this + Seattle in the core, you could run a Seattle game forever!<br /> <br /> The crossover section gives a very clear illustration of how the different supernaturals can intersect in one city (can't wait to see the analogue for Tokyo when glued together across the lines), the Mage with the visions was a nice touch.<br /> (Stray reminds me of Ein from Cowboy Bebop)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}